   title: Security/correctness: three verification-store reads swallow EVERY DB error with a bare `catch { }` and answer from an in-memory map — a DB outage reads as 'no such request'
   desc[:400]: ## BLUF  **Three functions backing the verification-upgrade surface swallow EVERY database error with a bare** `catch { /* fall through */ }` **and then answer from an in-memory map.** A DB failure is therefore indistinguishable from "no such request" — and worse than that, the route keeps answering, from process-local state that no other replica shares.  This is the **KS-963 swallow class**, not 
