KS-943 [Tested Not Deployed] High archived=None created=2026-09-06 PRs=['929']
   title: updateUser ignores rowCount and wallet.ts:511 discards its return — a 0-row UPDATE is reported as success (the RLS fail-closed case)
   desc[:400]: `updateUser` issues its UPDATE and **never checks that it matched a row**; `wallet.ts:511` discards the returned user and answers `{ success: true }` unconditionally. An UPDATE matching 0 rows is indistinguishable from one matching 1.  This is the residual of the class [[KS-720]] set out to close: the failure mode moved from *"no statement issued"* to *"statement issued, effect unverified"* — bett
